{
  "version": "0.2",
  "readme": {
    "note": "3D + simulation showcase: a small smart-factory monitoring model spanning every ArchiMate layer (General/Strategy/Business/Application/Technology/Data), two sections (Plant North / Plant South), and a real signal-flow simulation. Open Explore > 3D View to see it as a rotatable layered cube: each element group is its own Z-band, each type its own sub-layer, and the two Sections cluster their sensors/gateways into visually distinct bands within the Technology/Application layers. Click any cube to focus it and see its properties in the panel on the right; double-click (or keep zooming in on a focused cube) to jump to this same part on the 'factory-pipeline' 2D view. Then Step or Run Simulation (top toolbar) a few times: five Device sensors emit noisy periodic readings (watch their 3D markers turn blue and pulse most ticks -- 'changed' this tick), 'Vibration Sensor S1' intermittently drops offline (its marker flashes red every 5th tick -- a simulated fault), the two Sensor Gateways and Analytics Engine average their upstream readings (values take a few ticks to propagate through the whole chain, so Step several times or press Run). Once the combined risk score swings away from its own recent trend (e.g. right after that sensor fault recovers), the Analytics Engine raises an 'ANOMALY' badge (visible on the 2D canvas) and the Alerting Service logs an alert to the Message Log (left sidebar) -- an edge-triggered alert, so it logs once per swing, not once per tick. Everything not in the sensor chain (Actors, Capabilities, Goal, Driver, Process, Service) just shows a steady green 'normal' marker once simulation starts -- normal is a valid, common state too, not just filler."
  },
